# AI SQL Data Analyst (NovaCart, MySQL)

Ask a business question in plain English (e.g. *"Why did the iPhone 14 128GB not sell much?"*).
A local LLM (Ollama) plans the analysis, writes its own MySQL queries, validates and runs them, repairs its own
mistakes, and explains the result in plain language.

## Workflow

```
User question
   |
   v
[schema_inspector]  read the live MySQL schema (+ real values of small columns, date ranges)
   |
   v
[sql_analyst]       detect product / category in the question -> PLAN: 4-6 analysis steps (hypotheses)
   |
   v   (repeated for every step)
[sql_generator]     step -> one MySQL SELECT
   |
   v
[sql_validator]     SELECT-only? one statement? no forbidden words / system schemas?
   |                does MySQL accept it (EXPLAIN)?
   |  fail --------------------------+
   v                                 v
[query_executor]  --error / 0 rows-> [sql_repair]  (LLM fixes the query, up to 3 tries)
   |  rows
   v
[answer_generator]  all results -> short answer, evidence, causes, actions, caveats (in Rs)
   |
   v
app.py (Streamlit)  answer + every SQL query + result tables + charts
```

## Setup

```bash
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate            # Windows   (Mac/Linux: source venv/bin/activate)
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 1. MySQL must be running. Put your login in .env (MYSQL_USER / MYSQL_PASSWORD / MYSQL_DATABASE)

# 2. LLM (install Ollama from https://ollama.com first)
ollama pull llama3.1:8b          # or qwen2.5-coder:7b for stronger SQL

# 3. Fake data
python database/seed_data.py

# 4. App
streamlit run app.py
```

`seed_data.py` creates the database/tables from `schema.sql` only when they are missing (your own schema wins if
it already exists), empties the tables, and refills them. Re-running it is safe.

> `schema.sql` was written from the INSERT statements in your seed script. If your real tables have extra or
> differently named columns, the app still works (it reads the live schema); only the business rules in
> `src/sql_generator.py` (revenue, return rate...) mention column names such as `quantity`, `unit_price`,
> `item_discount`, `order_status`.

## The dataset (novacart, an Apple-products store)

8 categories, 48 products, 500 customers, 5,000 orders (all of 2025), ~10,000 order items, payments and returns.

| Category | Examples |
|---|---|
| iPhone | iPhone 16e, 16, 16 Plus, 16 Pro, 16 Pro Max (storage variants), iPhone 15, iPhone 14 |
| iPad | iPad (A16), iPad mini, iPad Air 11"/13", iPad Pro 11"/13" |
| Laptops | MacBook Air 13"/15", MacBook Pro 14"/16" (M4, M4 Pro, M4 Max, M5) |
| Desktops | iMac, Mac mini, Mac Studio |
| AirPods | AirPods 4, AirPods 4 ANC, AirPods Pro 2, AirPods Max |
| Apple Watch | SE, Series 10, Ultra 2 |
| Home & TV | Apple TV 4K, HomePod, HomePod mini |
| Accessories | Apple Pencil, Magic Mouse/Keyboard, AirTag, MagSafe Charger, USB-C adapter |

Product names and launch dates follow Apple's line-up; **prices are illustrative** rupee prices, not official.
A product never sells before its `launch_date`. To add or remove products, edit the `CATALOG` dictionary in
`database/seed_data.py` and re-run the script.

Four products are deliberately weak, each for a different reason, so you can check whether the AI finds the
truth. The seed script prints them and saves them to `database/underperformers.txt`; the app shows them as
example questions.

| Product | Hidden cause |
|---|---|
| iPhone 14 128GB | Demand shrinks ~22% every month (40 units in Jan, 2 in Dec) |
| AirPods Max | Priced ~3x the other AirPods, very few buyers |
| MagSafe Charger (1 m) | ~25% of delivered items returned, mostly Damaged / Not as Expected |
| MacBook Pro 14-inch (M5) | Launched 2025-10-22, so only ~2 months on sale |

## Safety

1. **Use a SELECT-only MySQL account for the AI** (strongly recommended):
   ```sql
   CREATE USER 'ai_reader'@'localhost' IDENTIFIED BY 'choose_a_password';
   GRANT SELECT ON novacart.* TO 'ai_reader'@'localhost';
   ```
   then set `MYSQL_RO_USER` / `MYSQL_RO_PASSWORD` in `.env`. The seed script keeps using `MYSQL_USER`.
2. Every AI session is also set to `READ ONLY`.
3. The validator allows one `SELECT`/`WITH` statement only and blocks `DROP`, `UPDATE`, `INTO OUTFILE`, `SLEEP`,
   access to `mysql` / `information_schema`, etc.
4. Row cap (`MAX_ROWS`) and time limit (`QUERY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS`) on every query.
5. Do not commit `.env` to Git.

## Tests

```bash
python -m pytest -v
```
The validator tests need nothing. The database/executor tests need MySQL + the seeded data and are skipped
automatically otherwise.

## Ideas to extend

- Add `reviews`, `marketing_campaigns` and `competitor_prices` tables: the planner will start using them
  automatically because it reads the live schema.
- Follow-up round: let the analyst read the first results and request extra queries.
- Conversation memory for follow-up questions.